::: {.cell-output-display}
![Normal force and braking torque from leading and trailing shoes in Example 4. Both shoes receive 350 N of actuating force from the same wheel cylinder, yet the leading shoe produces 19% more normal force due to the self-energizing effect.](02-11-Brakes_files/figure-epub/shoe-brake-comparison-14-1.png){fig-align='center'}
:::
