**Industry Application:** Tesla's one-pedal driving mode maximizes regenerative braking to the point where most city driving requires no friction brake application at all. The rear friction brakes on some Tesla Model 3 variants have been found to rust significantly because they are used so rarely — an unintended consequence of very aggressive regeneration. Tesla addressed this with a periodic friction brake application routine that automatically scrubs the rotors clean during low-speed driving.
:::

